From 102e3da7a0075e569b93f4749f9cc5541d65dbf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:13:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] Seer: Soulseek albums survive a failed track and never
 mix releases

A single failed transfer (size mismatch, peer refused) no longer fails the
whole album: the track is retried once and then fetched from another peer
that has the same album. The album is imported when at least half of it
arrived, with the missing tracks noted on the request. Albums are picked per
folder and in one format, so tracks of other releases by the same peer are
not pulled in. Stale transfer records are cleared before queueing, so a retry
doesn't read the previous attempt's state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

